    "reasoning": "The graph is strictly increasing on I and III, so each restriction is one-to-one and invertible. Interval II contains both increasing and decreasing portions, giving repeated function values. Current option 1 agrees with the earlier answer and MA's stated solution; the solution's extra space in \"I  and III only\" does not change its meaning. The solution also writes [-6,4] instead of [-6,4), but both intervals fail the horizontal line test, so this typo does not affect the answer.",
